  "_comment": "Hull catalog. Mounts own the arc: field is the sector list the mount can fire into (12 sectors of 30 degrees, 0 dead ahead, clockwise), families is what may be fitted, size caps the weapon size. base_load is what the bare hull consumes from each budget before weapons. mesh names the committed .obj the tactical view instances for this hull.",
  "_repairs": "damage_control is how fast the ship fixes itself and spare_parts is how much fixing it can pay for before it has to restock at a base. Federation Commander 5G1 gives a ship repair points every turn forever, because a scenario ends; ours is a ship that flies out and comes home, so the income becomes a stock that empties. Costs and durations per box live in data/tuning.json under repair. See docs/09-reference-federation-commander.md section 5.",
  "_internals": "Internals are grouped the way the ship systems display shows them and the way damage resolves. sectors is six lists, one per shield facing, numbered 1 to 6 from the bow clockwise, and each entry is [code, boxes, family] with an optional mount id linking a weapon to its mount so destroying the boxes disables it. core is the shared hull volume behind every facing: it has no shield of its own and only takes damage once the struck sector has nothing left, which is Federation Commander's hull rule generalised to six sections. See docs/09-reference-federation-commander.md.",
